17
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:32,977
Part one.

18
00:00:33,407 --> 00:00:35,380
The $77 math.

19
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,480
Damodaran first valued Anthropic on November 2nd.

20
00:00:38,828 --> 00:00:40,210
He told what he calls a big,

21
00:00:40,233 --> 00:00:41,383
uplifting story:

22
00:00:41,743 --> 00:00:43,879
a trillion dollars in revenue a year within

23
00:00:43,914 --> 00:00:44,854
about a decade,

24
00:00:45,214 --> 00:00:47,327
more than any company on earth makes today.

25
00:00:48,094 --> 00:00:50,474
Margins of 27.5%.

26
00:00:50,775 --> 00:00:53,492
A cost of capital of 9.7%.

27
00:00:53,841 --> 00:00:55,733
And one more step most people skip:

28
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,485
he treated the compute contracts like debt,

29
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,238
worth about $500 billion,

30
00:01:00,795 --> 00:01:01,967
and subtracted them.

31
00:01:02,316 --> 00:01:05,903
His answer was $1.475 trillion for the whole

32
00:01:05,938 --> 00:01:06,461
company.

33
00:01:06,937 --> 00:01:08,051
Then the world changed.

34
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,851
The midterm election,

35
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:12,835
he says, brought in a Congress more hostile

36
00:01:12,858 --> 00:01:14,936
to data centers and to AI.

37
00:01:15,296 --> 00:01:17,246
So he raised the cost of building compute

38
00:01:17,293 --> 00:01:19,104
and added a regulatory drag.

39
00:01:19,592 --> 00:01:21,182
That cut about $100 billion,

40
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,829
to roughly $1.35 trillion.

41
00:01:24,259 --> 00:01:25,617
Then he divided by the shares,

42
00:01:25,641 --> 00:01:27,347
including a big pile of options.

43
00:01:27,777 --> 00:01:30,644
His answer: $77 a share.

44
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:34,046
Moments later, the IPO priced at $83.

45
00:01:34,406 --> 00:01:37,262
His reaction: it terrifies me that I'm so

46
00:01:37,355 --> 00:01:38,795
close to a banker's price.

47
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:41,163
If you want the AI money story explained

48
00:01:41,187 --> 00:01:42,348
like this every week,

